# AGENTS.md — ${PROJECT_NAME}

Cross-tool agent guidance. Read by Codex CLI, Cursor, Aider, Continue, and other agentic tools that look for an `AGENTS.md` at the repo root.

## Workspace topology

This is the AI workspace of a dual-repo project. Production code lives in the sibling canonical repo (see `.workspace/pairing.json` for paths).

When running agentic tools here:
- Edits to MASTER-SPEC.md, memory-bank/, sprint specs land here (AI workspace).
- Edits to src/, tests/, PRD.md, SRS.md, ADRs land in canonical.
- See the `routing` block in `.workspace/pairing.json` for the full table.

## Git policy

- Commit messages must NOT contain AI-trace patterns (Co-Authored-By trailers, 🤖 markers). A `commit-msg` hook enforces this in both repos.
- Network ops (push/pull/fetch) require explicit user instruction. Default-deny per the manifest's `git_policy.allow_ai_*` fields.
- Local merges + rebases allowed.

## When in doubt

Read `CLAUDE.md` for the topology. Route lifecycle work through ossify: `/ossify:start` for an empty canonical and `/ossify:adopt` for existing source or history (on Codex, invoke the corresponding ossify skill).
